WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:06.220
Helmed by Damon Lindelof, HBO's Watchmen series
serves as a new and original story based within

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.120
the world created by Alan Moore and Dave Gibbons.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.160
And the cast members assembled for the show
are top-notch.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:16.560
From Academy Award winners to Coen Brothers
regulars, here's where you've probably seen

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.280
them before.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.880
Watchmen features active police officers who
wear masks while on duty to defend against

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.820
the Seventh Kalvary, a violent group inspired
by the original comic book's character Rorschach.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:32.580
Since members of the Kalvary wear masks that
mimic Rorschach's signature ink-blot look,

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:36.570
the police don masks as well, thanks to a
law that allows officers to hide their true

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:39.020
identities from those who might target them.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.860
One of those officers is Detective Angela
Abar, played by Regina King, who masquerades

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.839
under the identity of Sister Night.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.520
"I got a nose for white supremacy, and he
smells like bleach."

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.880
King has had a long and successful career
in Hollywood, which becomes clear when you

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.720
look at her slate of major awards.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.120
She's nabbed three Emmys and a Golden Globe,
and then she took home an Academy Award for

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.480
her supporting turn in 2018's If Beale Street
Could Talk.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.280
You might've also seen her in films like Boyz
n the Hood, in supporting TV roles on shows

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.910
like The Big Bang Theory, and as the star
of Netflix's short-lived Seven Seconds.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:18.050
For a little while, Jeremy Irons' role in
Watchmen was kept quiet, lending an air of

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.520
mystery to the proceedings.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.620
But ultimately an HBO featurette broke the
news about who he would be playing.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:29.160
The behind-the-scenes look featured cast interviews
referring to Irons as Ozymandias, a.k.a. Adrian

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:33.960
Veidt, a hugely important character from the
original comic known as the "World's Smartest

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:34.460
Man."

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:35.660
"Would you like it to occur to me, sir?"

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.320
"There are so many things I'd like to occur
to you.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:40.720
All right, dimwits.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.200
On with the show!"

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.020
Irons is one of a select number of performers
who have won the Triple Crown of Acting: an

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.780
Emmy, a Tony, and an Oscar.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.100
He's had an incredible career on the stage
and screen, and you've undoubtedly seen, or

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.140
heard, at least one of his acclaimed performances
over the years.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:01.710
One of his most famous performances only features
his voice, but even so, his turn as the villainous

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.350
Scar in The Lion King is unforgettable.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.869
Beyond the African plains, his notable roles
include Reversal of Fortune, for which he

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:12.200
won his Oscar, and Alfred Pennyworth in the
DCEU.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.480
In a world that requires constant protection
for police officers under attack from roving

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:22.049
terrorist groups, the police chief has to
be a powerful presence, protecting his officers

00:02:22.049 --> 00:02:24.880
from danger while still somehow trying to
keep the peace.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.580
In this version of Watchmen, that job falls
to Don Johnson as Chief Judd Crawford.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:33.740
Johnson has led an illustrious career, but
he might not be immediately recognizable to

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:34.540
younger viewers.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:38.860
Despite a few high-profile recent supporting
turns in movies like Django Unchained and

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:43.569
Book Club, he's undoubtedly best known for
his time as Sonny Crockett on Miami Vice,

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:48.220
the hit NBC detective show that ran from 1984
to 1989.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.540
These days, Johnson might be best known to
some people for his talented offspring, as

00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:57.040
his daughter Dakota Johnson has made a name
for herself in movies like Fifty Shades of

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.400
Grey and Bad Times at the El Royale.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.990
"I've had some ladies walk up to me and go,
'What do you think of your daughter in this

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:05.480
movie?'"

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.180
One of the new characters in this version
of Watchmen is known as Looking Glass, and

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.680
he's played by Tim Blake Nelson.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.900
He's a super-sharp cop with excellent interrogation
skills who might have a more sinister personality

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.540
lurking under the surface.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:21.240
In an interview on the Empire Podcast, Nelson
revealed,

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:24.500
"I don't really completely understand him,
and that's intentional.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:28.700
Damon Lindelof metes out facts about your
character as you go along...so I'm learning

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.150
as I go along who this guy is, and trying
to...It's almost like fresco painting.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.440
The clay is always wet."

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.300
"You know what strange means."

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.600
Luckily, Nelson is no stranger to complicated
characters.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:44.139
Some of his most notable roles include his
collaborations with fraternal filmmaking duo

00:03:44.139 --> 00:03:45.310
Joel and Ethan Coen.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:49.829
He played one of the escaped convicts in O
Brother, Where Art Thou? and the titular singing

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.180
cowboy in The Ballad of Buster Scruggs.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.099
He's also shown up on TV occasionally, including
memorable guest turns on the likes of Unbreakable

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:59.060
Kimmy Schmidt and Modern Family.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:05.320
An ideal way to connect Moore's Watchmen universe
to HBO's version is to feature familiar characters

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.260
who have aged since audiences last checked
in with them.

00:04:08.349 --> 00:04:11.819
So fans will likely be pleased to see Silk
Spectre once again.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:16.640
As played by Jean Smart, she's now working
as an FBI agent and going by the name Laurie

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:17.140
Blake.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.940
A formidable performer, Smart is the perfect
person for such an indispensable character.

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:27.780
From 1986 to 1991, she was best known for
her leading role on the popular CBS sitcom

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.720
Designing Women.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:33.180
Since then, she's continued an incredible
career, including roles on Frasier as an old

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:37.759
classmate of Frasier's and on 24 as the First
Lady of the United States.

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:42.540
In 2015, she appeared in the second season
of FX's Fargo, for which she nabbed the eighth

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.150
Emmy nomination of her career.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.740
Beyond the small screen, her film roles include
a small but crucial part in 2018's A Simple

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.240
Favor.

